course: dictionary
lesson: 5265
title: Journalist
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A journalist is a person whose job is to find out the news and tell it to other people. They write for newspapers, magazines and websites, or speak on TV, radio and online. «Some years ago some British newspaper journalists secretly listened to famous people's phone messages» shows the job in action: they were looking for a story.
explain: The sentence also shows that journalists must follow the law. «Which is against the law; they were caught, and it became a huge scandal» tells you that doing the job the wrong way causes trouble. A scandal is a shocking event that people talk about.
explain: Journalists can also be called reporters, who report the news, and editors, who check the stories before they are printed or shown. Read the words around a new word, such as «journalist», to see what job it describes.
fact: A journalist is a person whose job is to find out news and write or speak about it.
fact: Journalists work for newspapers, magazines, TV, radio or websites.
fact: In English lessons, you can write like a journalist: headlines, facts and quotes.
fact: Journalists must report the news truthfully, so people know what is really happening.
fact: Related words: reporter and editor.
exercise: What does a journalist do? | Builds houses from bricks | *Finds out news and writes or speaks about it | Cooks food in a restaurant kitchen | Looks after sick animals
exercise: In «journalists secretly listened to famous people's phone messages», what was against the law? | *Secretly listening to famous people's phone messages | Interviewing a football star | Writing a newspaper headline
exercise: Which related word also means a person who reports the news? | Pilot | Dentist | *Reporter | Gardener
test: Which place might a journalist work for? | A hospital ward | *A TV news channel | A shoe shop | A bakery
test: Why must a journalist report the news truthfully? | *So people know what is really happening | So the newspaper is printed in colour | So the story is longer | So nobody reads the news
exam: Which sentence best shows a journalist doing their job? | A journalist fixes the school roof | *A journalist writes a headline and quotes a witness for the newspaper | A journalist bakes bread for the café | A journalist plays in a football match
